# 小优引擎里程碑A 片8: dense_transformer HF 形状执行器切片 -- 独立 SUT/oracle
# 交叉验证 + 手工锚, 覆盖 model_executor.cheng::ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerOp
# 新增的 HF safetensors 形状派发分支 (qkv 4 权重 q/k/v/o -> 分离 GQA 投影,
# attention 1 权重 -> 真 paged-kv 硬 argmax 检索 + o_proj, mlp 3 权重
# gate/up/down -> SwiGLU, 以及全新的 residual_add 分支)。
#
# 缺口背景 (见 scratchpad/xiaoyou_planner_slice1.patch 文件头): 真 HF config
# (如 Qwen2.5) 喂进 hf_model_graph.HfModelGraphBuildDenseTransformerFromConfig
# 产出的图, 其算子权重 arity 与旧执行器 (照 ModelGraphBuildTinyDenseTransformerFixture
# 单权重惯例写) 完全不匹配, 任何 matmul 之前必死 "dense qkv: arity"。本文件验证
# 补丁后的新分支在真实的 (虽然是缩小合成的) HF 形状图上端到端正确, 且旧 tiny
# 单权重路径完全不受影响 (那部分由已有三个 smoke 覆盖: model_executor_dense_transformer_smoke.cheng
# / distributed_inference_engine_smoke.cheng / inference_dense_golden_ref_main.cheng,
# 三者在本切片补丁后逐位零回归, 见提交说明)。
#
# 合成 config: 2 层 / hidden=8 / attentionHeads=4 / keyValueHeads=2 (GQA 2:1,
# headDim 派生 = hidden/heads = 2) / intermediateSize=6 / vocab=6 / rope_theta
# =10000.0 / tie_word_embeddings=false -- 结构上是真 HfModelGraphBuildDenseTransformerFromConfig
# 产出 (真跑该函数, 不是手搭 ModelGraph 字面量), 只是维度缩到可手算规模 (对比
# 2026-07-13 规划器切片1 的真 Qwen2.5-0.5B config: hidden=896/24层/151936 词表,
# 那是端到端 plumbing 验证, 不是本文件这种可手工核对的单元级交叉验证)。
#
# 独立性契约: HfDgRef 前缀的每个函数都是从 model_executor.cheng 对应算子的
# 公开数学定义重新独立手写的 (embedding 查表/RmsNorm/transposed-weight 线性层/
# neox RoPE/GQA 硬 argmax paged 检索/SwiGLU/residual add), 本文件里只有
# main()/hfShapeBuildSutFixture()/hfShapeConfigJson()/sutCycleAt()/sutTakeStream()
# 这几个"搭 SUT 夹具"的函数导入并调用 cheng/inference/* -- 所有 HfDgRef* 函数体
# 内部零调用任何 cheng/inference/* 符号 (可用 grep 'HfDgRef' 与 grep 'mexec\.\|infer\.\|hfgraph\.\|ws\.\|wb\.\|engine\.' 交叉核对两者互斥)。
# sutCycleAt/HfDgRefCycleAt 是同一份确定性合成配方的两次独立实现 (同
# inference_dense_golden_ref_main.cheng 的 denseF16RawAt/DgRefCycleAt 关系一致:
# 共享的是"夹具惯例"数值本身, 不是算法), 图拓扑(算子序列/每层执行子步骤顺序)
# 同理是从 hf_model_graph.cheng 头部已读到的结构事实, 不是被测算法。
#
# 手工锚 (2026-07-13, 见文件末尾 main() 里对应断言, 数值均用 bash 整数四则/bc
# 三角函数复核过, 非临场心算): layer0 attention 算子的输出 (第一步 attention
# 输出, row1=第二个 prompt token), 逐算子链路:
#   embedding: hidden0 row1 = embed[token=2] (ordinals 16..23 of the 6-cycle
#     [1000,-500,250,4000,-2000,125]) = [-2000,125,1000,-500,250,4000,-2000,125]
#   rmsnorm(inputNorm=[1000,-500,250,4000,-2000,125,1000,-500], eps=1, scale=1000)
#     squareSum = 2000^2+125^2+1000^2+500^2+250^2+4000^2+2000^2+125^2 = 25343750
#     meanSquare = 25343750/8 = 3167968 (trunc); normBase = 3167968/1000 + 1 = 3168
#     norm0Out row1 = [-631,-19,78,-631,-157,157,-631,-19] (plain truncating
#     '/' per element, matches ModelExecutorRmsNormRowsFill exactly)
#   q = Linear(norm0Out row1, qW[8,8]) = [-939,3503,-3412,-939,3503,-3412,-939,3503]
#   k = Linear(norm0Out row1, kW[4,8]) = [-3412,-939,3503,-3412]
#   v = Linear(norm0Out row1, vW[4,8]) = [-939,3503,-3412,-939]
#     (Linear here is the transposed-weight [outFeatures,inFeatures] convention,
#     each inFeature term individually round-div'd by scale=1000 THEN summed --
#     matches ModelExecutorLinearOutInWeightFill exactly, NOT the plain
#     [inFeatures,outFeatures] DgRefMatMul convention the tiny fixture's own
#     qkv/mlp weights use)
#   RoPE (neox, headDim=2 -> halfDim=1 -> invFreq=[theta^0]=[1.0] always,
#     angle = position*1.0 radians; position=1: cos(1)=0.5403023058681397,
#     sin(1)=0.8414709848078965, scaled by trigScale=1073741824 and rounded ->
#     c=580145183, s=903522590):
#     q row1 per-head(dim2) rotate: head0[-939,3503]->[-3455,1103],
#       head1[-3412,-939]->[-1054,-3378], head2[3503,-3412]->[4764,1104],
#       head3[-939,3503]->[-3455,1103]
#       -> qRoped row1 = [-3455,1103,-1054,-3378,4764,1104,-3455,1103]
#     k row1 per-head(dim2) rotate: head0[-3412,-939]->[-1054,-3378],
#       head1[3503,-3412]->[4764,1104] -> kRoped row1 = [-1054,-3378,4764,1104]
#     (row0/position0 rotates to the identity exactly: cos(0)=1,sin(0)=0 are
#     exact, so qRoped row0=q row0, kRoped row0=k row0 -- no rounding at all)
#   [2026-07-18 #155 UPDATE: the paragraph below (originally derived
#   2026-07-13) described a GQA combined-representative-head hardmax
#   retrieval that is no longer what ModelExecutorPagedCausalAttentionFill's
#   CPU branch does. #153/#154 changed it: every attention head now keeps
#   its own query vector and its own independent 1/sqrt(headDim)-scaled
#   softmax distribution over causal candidates (paged_kv_cache.cheng's
#   PagedKVAttentionQueryFill, called with graph.attentionHeads query heads
#   and repeat=attentionHeads/keyValueHeads -- see
#   model_executor.cheng:838-852's own comment: "every attention head keeps
#   its own query vector and its own independent softmax distribution (HF
#   repeat_kv GQA semantics) -- heads sharing a kv-head group are NOT
#   collapsed into one distribution and broadcast"). The old
#   hardmax-and-broadcast paragraph, its combined-query-vector construction,
#   and its dot-product-only score are all stale and are kept below only as
#   a historical record of the pre-#153 formula this test used to pin down;
#   HfDgRefAttention has been rewritten (2026-07-18) to run the new
#   per-head-softmax algorithm and its output -- now
#   [-15353,55704,7379,-15353,55704,7379,-15353,55704] -- is what
#   `handAnchorRow1` below actually pins, verified against the real SUT's
#   "layer0.attention" tensor slot bit-for-bit by this file's own asserts,
#   not hand-expanded term-by-term here (the per-head loop, the 1/sqrt
#   fixed-point scale, and the 12-term Taylor softmax are mechanically
#   identical to inference_dense_golden_ref_main.cheng's DgRefCausalSoftmaxAttention
#   and paged_kv_cache_smoke.cheng's already hand-verified anchors -- see
#   those files for a fully expanded worked example of the same formula).]
#   GQA combined-representative-head hardmax retrieval (STALE, pre-#153 --
#   mirrors ModelExecutorGroupedQueryVectorFill + PagedKVAttentionQueryFill's
#   pre-#153 form: ONE combined width-kvRows query vector per token, taking
#   each kv head's FIRST query head (queryHead=kvHead*repeat, repeat=4/2=2)
#   -- NOT independent per-kv-head retrieval; the "attention" was a single
#   raw dot-product hardmax pick per token, not softmax):
#     combined query (row1) = [qRoped head0, qRoped head2] = [-3455,1103,4764,1104]
#     candidate0 (token0, kRoped row0=[1783,-3585,-636,1783]):
#       score0 = -3455*1783 + 1103*-3585 + 4764*-636 + 1104*1783 = -11175992
#     candidate1 (token1/self, kRoped row1=[-1054,-3378,4764,1104]):
#       score1 = -3455*-1054 + 1103*-3378 + 4764*4764 + 1104*1104 = 23830148
#     score1 > score0 -> hardmax winner = token1 (self); groupedOut = v row1
#       = [-939,3503,-3412,-939] (v is never rotated by RoPE)
#     broadcast winner's per-kv-head slice to its repeat=2 query heads:
#       queryHead0=queryHead1 <- groupedOut[0:2]=[-939,3503]
#       queryHead2=queryHead3 <- groupedOut[2:4]=[-3412,-939]
#       -> context row1 = [-939,3503,-939,3503,-3412,-939,-3412,-939]
#     o_proj = Linear(context row1, oW[8,8]) -> pre-#153 attn0 row1 =
#       [1723,14851,8542,1723,14851,8542,1723,14851] (superseded, see
#       2026-07-18 update above)
# The current (post-#153/#154) row1 vector is asserted three ways below:
# (1) against `handAnchorRow1`, (2) against HfDgRefAttention's
# independently-coded result, (3) against the real SUT's
# ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerOp op-by-op replay reading the
# "layer0.attention" tensor slot straight out of the executor -- a genuine
# intermediate-tensor (not just final-logits) bit-for-bit cross-check,
# matching the milestone brief's "关键中间张量逐位" requirement.

const
    HfDgRefScale: int32 = 1000
    HfDgRefTrigScale: int32 = 1073741824
    HfDgRefSoftmaxScale: int32 = 10000

fn HfDgRefRopeTheta(): float64 =
    return 10000.0

# Same deterministic synthetic cycle convention as
# inference_dense_golden_ref_main.cheng's DgRefCycleAt / model_executor_dense_transformer_smoke.cheng's
# denseF16RawAt (a shared fixture convention, independently re-typed here --
# see the independence-contract header comment above).
fn HfDgRefCycleAt(ordinal: int32): int32 =
    let slot = ordinal % 6
    if slot == 0:
        return 1000
    if slot == 1:
        return -500
    if slot == 2:
        return 250
    if slot == 3:
        return 4000
    if slot == 4:
        return -2000
    return 125

fn HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal: var int32, count: int32): int32[] =
    var out: int32[]
    for _ in 0..<count:
        add(out, HfDgRefCycleAt(ordinal))
        ordinal = ordinal + 1
    return out

type
    HfDgRefMat =
        rows: int32
        cols: int32
        vals: int32[]

fn HfDgRefOffset(cols: int32, row: int32, col: int32): int32 =
    return row * cols + col

fn HfDgRefSat(value: int64): int32 =
    if value > int64(2147483647):
        return 2147483647
    if value < int64(-2147483648):
        return -2147483648
    return int32(value)

fn HfDgRefRoundDiv(numer: int64, denom: int64): int64 =
    if denom <= int64(0):
        return int64(0)
    let half = denom / int64(2)
    if numer >= int64(0):
        return (numer + half) / denom
    return (numer - half) / denom

# Integer sqrt via Newton's method, mirroring infer.InferenceIntSqrt
# (kernel.cheng) exactly.
fn HfDgRefIntSqrt(value: int64): int64 =
    if value <= int64(0):
        return int64(0)
    var x = value
    var y = (x + int64(1)) / int64(2)
    while y < x:
        x = y
        y = (x + value / x) / int64(2)
    return x

fn HfDgRefMulQ(a: int32, b: int32, scale: int32): int32 =
    let product = int64(a) * int64(b)
    return HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(product, int64(scale)))

fn HfDgRefEmbedding(tokenIds: int32[], emb: HfDgRefMat): HfDgRefMat =
    let tokenCount = tokenIds.len
    let hidden = emb.cols
    var outVals: int32[]
    for _ in 0..<(tokenCount * hidden):
        add(outVals, 0)
    for t in 0..<tokenCount:
        let tokenId = tokenIds[t]
        for h in 0..<hidden:
            outVals[HfDgRefOffset(hidden, t, h)] = emb.vals[HfDgRefOffset(hidden, tokenId, h)]
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: tokenCount, cols: hidden, vals: outVals)

fn HfDgRefRmsNormRows(x: HfDgRefMat, weight: int32[], epsilonScale: int32): HfDgRefMat =
    var outVals: int32[]
    for _ in 0..<x.vals.len:
        add(outVals, 0)
    for t in 0..<x.rows:
        var squareSum: int64
        for h in 0..<x.cols:
            let v = x.vals[HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, t, h)]
            squareSum = squareSum + int64(v) * int64(v)
        let meanSquare = squareSum / int64(x.cols)
        # #153/#154 root fix mirrored here: normBase is the fixed-point sqrt
        # of (meanSquare + epsilonScale), not a truncated-divide-by-scale --
        # matches ModelExecutorRmsNormRowsFill exactly (model_executor.cheng:918).
        var normBase = HfDgRefIntSqrt(meanSquare + int64(epsilonScale))
        if normBase <= int64(0):
            normBase = int64(1)
        for h in 0..<x.cols:
            let inputValue = x.vals[HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, t, h)]
            let weightValue = weight[h]
            let weighted = int64(inputValue) * int64(weightValue)
            outVals[HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, t, h)] = HfDgRefSat(weighted / normBase)
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: x.rows, cols: x.cols, vals: outVals)

# Transposed-weight ([outFeatures,inFeatures], real safetensors/nn.Linear
# layout) linear layer: #153 root fix mirrored here -- the full-precision
# int64 dot product is accumulated across every inFeature term first, then
# round-divided by scale exactly once at the end -- mirrors
# ModelExecutorLinearOutInWeightFill exactly (model_executor.cheng:1029-1037).
# This is a different weight-layout convention from the tiny fixture's own
# [inFeatures,outFeatures] plain-matmul qkv/mlp weights (see file header).
fn HfDgRefLinear(x: HfDgRefMat, w: HfDgRefMat): HfDgRefMat =
    var outVals: int32[]
    for row in 0..<x.rows:
        for outF in 0..<w.rows:
            var sum: int64
            for inF in 0..<x.cols:
                let product = int64(x.vals[HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, row, inF)]) *
                              int64(w.vals[HfDgRefOffset(w.cols, outF, inF)])
                sum = sum + product
            add(outVals, HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(sum, int64(HfDgRefScale))))
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: x.rows, cols: w.rows, vals: outVals)

# Prefill-only per-head neox RoPE (position == row index, no kv-cache carry-in
# -- ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerTokens takes no kv-state param, full
# recompute every generate step, so basePosition is always 0 in production
# too). Rotates every `headCount` consecutive headDim-wide column span in
# each row. Mirrors ModelExecutorRopeApplyQkFill's per-head loop (generalized
# to any headCount, covering both the attentionHeads-many q heads and the
# keyValueHeads-many k heads).
fn HfDgRefRopeApplyHeads(x: HfDgRefMat, headCount: int32, headDim: int32, theta: float64): HfDgRefMat =
    let halfDim = headDim / 2
    var outVals: int32[]
    for i in 0..<x.vals.len:
        add(outVals, x.vals[i])
    let lnTheta = mathlib.Ln(theta)
    var invFreq: float64[]
    for j in 0..<halfDim:
        let exponent = 0.0 - float64(2 * j) / float64(2 * halfDim)
        add(invFreq, mathlib.Exp(exponent * lnTheta))
    let trigScaleF = float64(HfDgRefTrigScale)
    for row in 0..<x.rows:
        var cosRow: int32[]
        var sinRow: int32[]
        for j in 0..<halfDim:
            let angle = float64(row) * invFreq[j]
            add(cosRow, int32(int64(mathlib.Round(mathlib.Cos(angle) * trigScaleF))))
            add(sinRow, int32(int64(mathlib.Round(mathlib.Sin(angle) * trigScaleF))))
        for head in 0..<headCount:
            let colStart = head * headDim
            for j in 0..<halfDim:
                let idx1 = HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, row, colStart + j)
                let idx2 = HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, row, colStart + halfDim + j)
                let x1 = outVals[idx1]
                let x2 = outVals[idx2]
                let c = cosRow[j]
                let s = sinRow[j]
                let o1 = HfDgRefSat(int64(HfDgRefMulQ(x1, c, HfDgRefTrigScale)) - int64(HfDgRefMulQ(x2, s, HfDgRefTrigScale)))
                let o2 = HfDgRefSat(int64(HfDgRefMulQ(x2, c, HfDgRefTrigScale)) + int64(HfDgRefMulQ(x1, s, HfDgRefTrigScale)))
                outVals[idx1] = o1
                outVals[idx2] = o2
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: x.rows, cols: x.cols, vals: outVals)

# GQA causal attention: mirrors ModelExecutorPagedCausalAttentionFill +
# ModelExecutorGroupedQueryVectorFill + PagedKVAttentionQueryFill +
# ModelExecutorWriteGroupedValueToHiddenRow exactly. Production is NOT
# softmax attention and NOT independent per-kv-head retrieval: it builds one
# combined width-kvRows query vector per token (each kv head contributes only
# its FIRST query head's slice), does a single raw-dot-product HARDMAX pick
# (strict '>', ties keep the earliest candidate) against every causal
# candidate's full kvRows-wide key, then broadcasts the winning candidate's
# full kvRows-wide value back out, per kv head, to every query head in that
# kv head's group. This is pre-existing shared production code (unmodified
# by this milestone's patch); this oracle reproduces it byte-for-byte, not a
# "textbook" independent-multi-head-softmax attention.
# #153/#154 root fix mirrored here: every attention head keeps its own
# query vector and its own independent 1/sqrt(headDim)-scaled softmax
# distribution over causal candidates (HF repeat_kv GQA semantics) -- heads
# sharing a kv-head group are NOT collapsed into one hardmax pick and
# broadcast. Mirrors paged_kv_cache.cheng's PagedKVAttentionQueryFill
# exactly (as invoked from ModelExecutorPagedCausalAttentionFill's CPU
# branch, model_executor.cheng:838-852), specialized to attend over the
# causal candidate rows 0..t already computed here as full matrices, since
# this oracle has no separate paged-cache append step.
fn HfDgRefAttention(qRoped: HfDgRefMat, kRoped: HfDgRefMat, v: HfDgRefMat, oW: HfDgRefMat,
                    attentionHeads: int32, keyValueHeads: int32, headDim: int32): HfDgRefMat =
    let repeat = attentionHeads / keyValueHeads
    let hidden = attentionHeads * headDim
    let sqrtFix: int64 = int64(10000)
    let isqrtHead = HfDgRefIntSqrt(int64(headDim) * sqrtFix * sqrtFix)
    var contextVals: int32[]
    for _ in 0..<(qRoped.rows * hidden):
        add(contextVals, 0)
    for t in 0..<qRoped.rows:
        for qh in 0..<attentionHeads:
            let kvHead = qh / repeat
            let queryBase = qh * headDim
            let kvBase = kvHead * headDim
            var scores: int32[]
            var maxScore: int32
            var sawCandidate: bool
            for c in 0..<t + 1:
                var dot: int64
                for d in 0..<headDim:
                    dot = dot + int64(qRoped.vals[HfDgRefOffset(qRoped.cols, t, queryBase + d)]) *
                                int64(kRoped.vals[HfDgRefOffset(kRoped.cols, c, kvBase + d)])
                let score = HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(dot * sqrtFix, int64(HfDgRefScale) * isqrtHead))
                if !sawCandidate || score > maxScore:
                    maxScore = score
                    sawCandidate = true
                add(scores, score)
            var weights: int32[]
            var denom: int64
            for i in 0..<scores.len:
                let weight = HfDgRefExpNegQ(scores[i] - maxScore, HfDgRefScale, HfDgRefSoftmaxScale)
                add(weights, weight)
                denom = denom + int64(weight)
            for d in 0..<headDim:
                var numer: int64
                for c in 0..<t + 1:
                    numer = numer + int64(v.vals[HfDgRefOffset(v.cols, c, kvBase + d)]) * int64(weights[c])
                contextVals[HfDgRefOffset(hidden, t, queryBase + d)] = HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(numer, denom))
    let context = HfDgRefMat(rows: qRoped.rows, cols: hidden, vals: contextVals)
    return HfDgRefLinear(context, oW)

# #153 root fix mirrored here: q/k/v projection bias, row-wise add per
# output feature -- mirrors ModelExecutorAddBiasRows exactly
# (model_executor.cheng:986-1005).
fn HfDgRefAddBiasRows(x: HfDgRefMat, bias: int32[]): HfDgRefMat =
    var outVals: int32[]
    for row in 0..<x.rows:
        for f in 0..<x.cols:
            let off = HfDgRefOffset(x.cols, row, f)
            add(outVals, HfDgRefSat(int64(x.vals[off]) + int64(bias[f])))
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: x.rows, cols: x.cols, vals: outVals)

fn HfDgRefResidualAdd(a: HfDgRefMat, b: HfDgRefMat): HfDgRefMat =
    var outVals: int32[]
    for i in 0..<a.vals.len:
        add(outVals, HfDgRefSat(int64(a.vals[i]) + int64(b.vals[i])))
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: a.rows, cols: a.cols, vals: outVals)

# Same 12-term fixed-point Taylor series identity as
# inference_dense_golden_ref_main.cheng's DgRefExpNegQ / model_executor.cheng's
# InferenceExpNegQ, independently re-typed (see independence-contract header).
fn HfDgRefExpNegQ(delta: int32, inputScale: int32, outputScale: int32): int32 =
    if delta >= 0:
        return outputScale
    if delta <= 0 - inputScale * 8:
        return 0
    let dQ = HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(0 - delta) * int64(outputScale), int64(inputScale)))
    var term: int64 = int64(outputScale)
    var total: int64 = int64(outputScale)
    for k in 1..12:
        term = HfDgRefRoundDiv(term * int64(dQ), int64(outputScale * k))
        total = total + term
    if total <= int64(0):
        return 0
    return HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(outputScale) * int64(outputScale), total))

# sigmoid(x) = 1/(1+exp(-x)) in HfDgRefScale fixed point, mirrors
# ModelExecutorSigmoidQ exactly (both branches, split at value>=0 the same
# way for numerical stability -- see that function's own comment).
fn HfDgRefSigmoidQ(value: int32, scale: int32): int32 =
    var expTerm: int32
    if value >= 0:
        expTerm = HfDgRefExpNegQ(0 - value, scale, scale)
        let denom = int64(scale) + int64(expTerm)
        return HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(scale) * int64(scale), denom))
    expTerm = HfDgRefExpNegQ(value, scale, scale)
    let denom = int64(scale) + int64(expTerm)
    return HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(expTerm) * int64(scale), denom))

# SwiGLU(gate,up) = up * SiLU(gate), SiLU(x) = x*sigmoid(x). Mirrors
# ModelExecutorSwiGluFill exactly.
fn HfDgRefSwiGlu(gate: HfDgRefMat, up: HfDgRefMat): HfDgRefMat =
    var outVals: int32[]
    for i in 0..<gate.vals.len:
        let sigmoid = HfDgRefSigmoidQ(gate.vals[i], HfDgRefScale)
        let silu = HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(gate.vals[i]) * int64(sigmoid), int64(HfDgRefScale)))
        add(outVals, HfDgRefSat(HfDgRefRoundDiv(int64(silu) * int64(up.vals[i]), int64(HfDgRefScale))))
    return HfDgRefMat(rows: gate.rows, cols: gate.cols, vals: outVals)

type
    HfDgRefLayerWeights =
        inputNorm: int32[]
        qW: HfDgRefMat
        kW: HfDgRefMat
        vW: HfDgRefMat
        oW: HfDgRefMat
        qBias: int32[]
        kBias: int32[]
        vBias: int32[]
        postNorm: int32[]
        gateW: HfDgRefMat
        upW: HfDgRefMat
        downW: HfDgRefMat

    HfDgRefWeights =
        emb: HfDgRefMat
        layers: HfDgRefLayerWeights[]
        finalNorm: int32[]
        lmHeadW: HfDgRefMat

# Weight order mirrors HfModelGraphBuildDenseTransformerFromConfig's
# graph.weights list exactly (embed -> per layer [inputNorm, q, k, v, o,
# qBias, kBias, vBias, postNorm, gate, up, down] -> finalNorm -> lmHead,
# tie_word_embeddings=false so lmHead is its own shard) -- a structural
# fixture fact, not the algorithm under test (see file header). #153 added
# the per-layer q/k/v projection biases (hf_model_graph.cheng:2442-2453,
# self_attn.{q,k,v}_proj.bias), which is the real +6 weights (3 biases x 2
# layers) behind the "21 -> 27" inventory count re-derivation below.
fn HfDgRefBuildWeights(layerCount: int32, hiddenSize: int32, kvRows: int32,
                       intermediateSize: int32, vocabSize: int32): HfDgRefWeights =
    var ordinal: int32
    let embVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, vocabSize * hiddenSize)
    var layers: HfDgRefLayerWeights[]
    for _ in 0..<layerCount:
        let inputNorm = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize)
        let qVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize * hiddenSize)
        let kVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, kvRows * hiddenSize)
        let vVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, kvRows * hiddenSize)
        let oVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize * hiddenSize)
        let qBias = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize)
        let kBias = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, kvRows)
        let vBias = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, kvRows)
        let postNorm = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize)
        let gateVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, intermediateSize * hiddenSize)
        let upVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, intermediateSize * hiddenSize)
        let downVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize * intermediateSize)
        add(layers, HfDgRefLayerWeights(
            inputNorm: inputNorm,
            qW: HfDgRefMat(rows: hiddenSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: qVals),
            kW: HfDgRefMat(rows: kvRows, cols: hiddenSize, vals: kVals),
            vW: HfDgRefMat(rows: kvRows, cols: hiddenSize, vals: vVals),
            oW: HfDgRefMat(rows: hiddenSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: oVals),
            qBias: qBias,
            kBias: kBias,
            vBias: vBias,
            postNorm: postNorm,
            gateW: HfDgRefMat(rows: intermediateSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: gateVals),
            upW: HfDgRefMat(rows: intermediateSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: upVals),
            downW: HfDgRefMat(rows: hiddenSize, cols: intermediateSize, vals: downVals)
        ))
    let finalNorm = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, hiddenSize)
    let lmHeadVals = HfDgRefTakeStream(ordinal, vocabSize * hiddenSize)
    return HfDgRefWeights(
        emb: HfDgRefMat(rows: vocabSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: embVals),
        layers: layers,
        finalNorm: finalNorm,
        lmHeadW: HfDgRefMat(rows: vocabSize, cols: hiddenSize, vals: lmHeadVals)
    )

# Op sequence per layer mirrors ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerOp's new
# HF-shape dispatch order exactly: RmsNorm(input) -> Qkv(4w) -> Rope(qk-split)
# -> Attention(1w, GQA) -> ResidualAdd -> RmsNorm(post) -> Mlp(3w, SwiGLU) ->
# ResidualAdd.
fn HfDgRefLayerForward(x: HfDgRefMat, w: HfDgRefLayerWeights,
                       attentionHeads: int32, keyValueHeads: int32, headDim: int32,
                       theta: float64): HfDgRefMat =
    let normed = HfDgRefRmsNormRows(x, w.inputNorm, 1)
    let q = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(normed, w.qW), w.qBias)
    let k = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(normed, w.kW), w.kBias)
    let v = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(normed, w.vW), w.vBias)
    let qRoped = HfDgRefRopeApplyHeads(q, attentionHeads, headDim, theta)
    let kRoped = HfDgRefRopeApplyHeads(k, keyValueHeads, headDim, theta)
    let attnOut = HfDgRefAttention(qRoped, kRoped, v, w.oW, attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim)
    let attnResidual = HfDgRefResidualAdd(x, attnOut)
    let postNormed = HfDgRefRmsNormRows(attnResidual, w.postNorm, 1)
    let gate = HfDgRefLinear(postNormed, w.gateW)
    let up = HfDgRefLinear(postNormed, w.upW)
    let activated = HfDgRefSwiGlu(gate, up)
    let mlpOut = HfDgRefLinear(activated, w.downW)
    return HfDgRefResidualAdd(attnResidual, mlpOut)

fn HfDgRefForward(tokenIds: int32[], w: HfDgRefWeights,
                  attentionHeads: int32, keyValueHeads: int32, headDim: int32,
                  theta: float64): HfDgRefMat =
    var hidden = HfDgRefEmbedding(tokenIds, w.emb)
    for i in 0..<w.layers.len:
        hidden = HfDgRefLayerForward(hidden, w.layers[i], attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim, theta)
    let normed = HfDgRefRmsNormRows(hidden, w.finalNorm, 1)
    return HfDgRefLinear(normed, w.lmHeadW)

fn HfDgRefArgmaxRow(logits: HfDgRefMat, row: int32): int32 =
    var bestIndex: int32
    var bestValue = logits.vals[HfDgRefOffset(logits.cols, row, 0)]
    for c in 1..<logits.cols:
        let v = logits.vals[HfDgRefOffset(logits.cols, row, c)]
        if v > bestValue:
            bestValue = v
            bestIndex = c
    return bestIndex

# Algorithm-independent re-derivation of DistributedGenerateGreedyDenseTransformerTokens's
# contract: no persisted kv cache, full forward recompute every step over the
# whole token list so far, next token = argmax over the last row's logits.
fn HfDgRefGenerateGreedy(promptTokenIds: int32[], maxNewTokens: int32, eosTokenId: int32,
                         w: HfDgRefWeights, attentionHeads: int32, keyValueHeads: int32,
                         headDim: int32, theta: float64): int32[] =
    var current: int32[]
    for i in 0..<promptTokenIds.len:
        add(current, promptTokenIds[i])
    for _ in 0..<maxNewTokens:
        let logits = HfDgRefForward(current, w, attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim, theta)
        let lastRow = current.len - 1
        let token = HfDgRefArgmaxRow(logits, lastRow)
        add(current, token)
        if eosTokenId >= 0 && token == eosTokenId:
            break
    return current

fn HfDgRefIntArrayToString(arr: int32[]): str =
    var parts: str[]
    for i in 0..<arr.len:
        add(parts, strings.IntToStr(arr[i]))
    return strutil.Join(parts, ",")

# ============ SUT-side setup (this half imports cheng/inference/*) ============

fn hfShapeConfigJson(): str =
    return strutil.Join([
        "{",
        "\"architectures\":[\"Qwen2ForCausalLM\"],",
        "\"model_type\":\"qwen2\",",
        "\"vocab_size\":6,",
        "\"hidden_size\":8,",
        "\"num_hidden_layers\":2,",
        "\"num_attention_heads\":4,",
        "\"num_key_value_heads\":2,",
        "\"intermediate_size\":6,",
        "\"tie_word_embeddings\":false,",
        "\"rope_theta\":10000.0",
        "}"
    ], "")

# Independently re-typed instance of the same 6-value cycle as HfDgRefCycleAt
# (shared fixture convention, not shared algorithm -- see file header).
fn sutCycleAt(ordinal: int32): int32 =
    let slot = ordinal % 6
    if slot == 0:
        return 1000
    if slot == 1:
        return -500
    if slot == 2:
        return 250
    if slot == 3:
        return 4000
    if slot == 4:
        return -2000
    return 125

fn sutTakeStream(ordinal: var int32, count: int32): int32[] =
    var out: int32[]
    for _ in 0..<count:
        add(out, sutCycleAt(ordinal))
        ordinal = ordinal + 1
    return out

type
    HfShapeSutFixture =
        graph: mg.ModelGraph
        bindings: wb.WeightBindingSet
        store: ws.WeightTensorStore

fn hfShapeBuildSutFixture(): HfShapeSutFixture =
    let graphRes = hfgraph.HfModelGraphBuildDenseTransformerFromConfig(
        hfShapeConfigJson(),
        "cid:model:dense-hf-shape-golden-ref",
        kir.KernelDtypeFp16,
        mg.ModelQuantSchemeNone
    )
    assert(IsOk(graphRes), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: build graph")
    let graph = Value(graphRes)
    assert(IsOk(mg.ModelGraphValidate(graph)), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: graph valid")
    assert(graph.architecture == mg.InferenceModelArchitectureDenseTransformer &&
           graph.weights.len == 27 && graph.ops.len == 19 &&
           graph.hiddenSize == 8 && graph.attentionHeads == 4 &&
           graph.keyValueHeads == 2 && graph.headDim == 2 && graph.layerCount == 2,
           " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: graph inventory (real HF-shape dims)")

    var ordinal: int32
    var payloads: ws.WeightTensorPayload[]
    var bindings: wb.WeightShardBinding[]
    for i in 0..<graph.weights.len:
        let countRes = mg.ModelGraphTensorElementCount(graph.weights[i].shape)
        assert(IsOk(countRes), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: weight element count")
        let elemCount = int32(Value(countRes))
        let data = sutTakeStream(ordinal, elemCount)
        var tensor: infer.TensorQ
        let fillOk = infer.TensorFromDataFill(tensor, graph.weights[i].shape, HfDgRefScale, data)
        assert(IsOk(fillOk), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: weight tensor fill")
        let peerId = strutil.Join(["peer:dense-hf-shape:", strings.IntToStr(i)], "")
        let payloadRes = ws.WeightTensorPayloadBuild(
            graph.weights[i].modelCid,
            graph.weights[i].tensorName,
            graph.weights[i].shardCid,
            graph.weights[i].dtype,
            graph.weights[i].quantScheme,
            peerId,
            tensor
        )
        assert(IsOk(payloadRes), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: weight payload")
        let payload = Value(payloadRes)
        add(payloads, payload)
        add(bindings, wb.WeightShardBinding(
            modelCid: graph.weights[i].modelCid,
            tensorName: graph.weights[i].tensorName,
            shardCid: graph.weights[i].shardCid,
            dtype: graph.weights[i].dtype,
            quantScheme: graph.weights[i].quantScheme,
            sizeBytes: graph.weights[i].sizeBytes,
            peerId: peerId,
            payloadHash: payload.payloadHash
        ))
    let set = wb.WeightBindingBuildSet(graph.modelCid, bindings)
    let store = ws.WeightTensorStoreBuild(graph.modelCid, payloads)
    var hashes: int64[]
    for i in 0..<payloads.len:
        add(hashes, payloads[i].payloadHash)
    let boundGraphRes = mg.ModelGraphBindExpectedWeightPayloadHashes(graph, hashes)
    assert(IsOk(boundGraphRes), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: bind weight anchors")
    let boundGraph = Value(boundGraphRes)
    assert(IsOk(wb.WeightBindingValidate(set, boundGraph)), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: weight bindings")
    assert(IsOk(ws.WeightTensorValidateStore(store, set, boundGraph)), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: weight store")
    return HfShapeSutFixture(graph: boundGraph, bindings: set, store: store)

# Manual op-by-op replay (same public ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerOp
# calls ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerTokens's own loop makes
# internally) so this test can read the "layer0.attention" intermediate
# tensor straight out of the executor's tensor slots -- the "关键中间张量逐位"
# cross-check, not just a final-logits comparison.
fn hfShapeReplayOps(graph: mg.ModelGraph, store: ws.WeightTensorStore,
                    tokenIds: infer.TensorQ): mexec.ModelExecutorTensorSlot[] =
    var slots: mexec.ModelExecutorTensorSlot[]
    let putToken = mexec.ModelExecutorPutTensor(slots, "token_ids", tokenIds)
    assert(IsOk(putToken), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: put token ids")
    var executionHash: int64
    for i in 0..<graph.ops.len:
        let opOk = mexec.ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerOp(graph, store, graph.ops[i], slots, executionHash)
        if IsErr(opOk):
            echo(strutil.Join(["op replay failed at i=", strings.IntToStr(i), " opKind=", graph.ops[i].opKind,
                                " out=", graph.ops[i].outputName, " err=", Error(opOk)], ""))
        assert(IsOk(opOk), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: op replay")
    return slots

fn main(): int32 =
    let fixture = hfShapeBuildSutFixture()
    let graph = fixture.graph
    let attentionHeads: int32 = 4
    let keyValueHeads: int32 = 2
    let headDim: int32 = 2
    let hiddenSize: int32 = 8
    let kvRows = keyValueHeads * headDim
    let intermediateSize: int32 = 6
    let vocabSize: int32 = 6
    let layerCount: int32 = 2

    var promptTokenIds: infer.TensorQ
    let promptOk = infer.TensorFromDataFill(promptTokenIds, [2], 1, [1, 2])
    assert(IsOk(promptOk), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: prompt tensor build")

    # --- independent oracle forward pass ---
    let oracleWeights = HfDgRefBuildWeights(layerCount, hiddenSize, kvRows, intermediateSize, vocabSize)
    let oraclePromptIds = [1, 2]
    let oracleLogits = HfDgRefForward(oraclePromptIds, oracleWeights, attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim, HfDgRefRopeTheta())
    echo(strutil.Join(["oracle logits: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString(oracleLogits.vals)], ""))

    # --- hand-derivation anchor: layer0's attention op OUTPUT at row1, cross
    # -checked against (1) HfDgRefAttention directly and (2) the SUT's own
    # "layer0.attention" tensor slot below ---
    let handAnchorRow1 = [-15353, 55704, 7379, -15353, 55704, 7379, -15353, 55704]
    let oracleNorm0 = HfDgRefRmsNormRows(HfDgRefEmbedding(oraclePromptIds, oracleWeights.emb), oracleWeights.layers[0].inputNorm, 1)
    let oracleQ0 = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(oracleNorm0, oracleWeights.layers[0].qW), oracleWeights.layers[0].qBias)
    let oracleK0 = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(oracleNorm0, oracleWeights.layers[0].kW), oracleWeights.layers[0].kBias)
    let oracleV0 = HfDgRefAddBiasRows(HfDgRefLinear(oracleNorm0, oracleWeights.layers[0].vW), oracleWeights.layers[0].vBias)
    let oracleQRoped0 = HfDgRefRopeApplyHeads(oracleQ0, attentionHeads, headDim, HfDgRefRopeTheta())
    let oracleKRoped0 = HfDgRefRopeApplyHeads(oracleK0, keyValueHeads, headDim, HfDgRefRopeTheta())
    let oracleAttn0 = HfDgRefAttention(oracleQRoped0, oracleKRoped0, oracleV0, oracleWeights.layers[0].oW, attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim)
    echo(strutil.Join(["oracle layer0 attention row1: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString(oracleAttn0.vals)], ""))
    for c in 0..<8:
        assert(oracleAttn0.vals[HfDgRefOffset(8, 1, c)] == handAnchorRow1[c],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: hand-derivation anchor vs independent oracle")

    # --- SUT op-by-op replay: read the same "layer0.attention" tensor
    # straight out of the production executor ---
    let slots = hfShapeReplayOps(graph, fixture.store, promptTokenIds)
    let sutLayer0Attn = mexec.ModelExecutorFindTensor(slots, "layer0.attention")
    assert(IsOk(sutLayer0Attn), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: find layer0.attention slot")
    let sutAttn0 = Value(sutLayer0Attn)
    assert(sutAttn0.shape.len == 2 && sutAttn0.shape[0] == 2 && sutAttn0.shape[1] == 8,
           " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut layer0.attention shape")
    echo(strutil.Join(["sut layer0 attention row1: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString([
        sutAttn0.data[8], sutAttn0.data[9], sutAttn0.data[10], sutAttn0.data[11],
        sutAttn0.data[12], sutAttn0.data[13], sutAttn0.data[14], sutAttn0.data[15]
    ])], ""))
    for c in 0..<8:
        assert(sutAttn0.data[8 + c] == handAnchorRow1[c],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: hand-derivation anchor vs SUT intermediate tensor")
        assert(sutAttn0.data[8 + c] == oracleAttn0.vals[HfDgRefOffset(8, 1, c)],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: SUT intermediate tensor vs independent oracle")

    let sutLogitsTensor = mexec.ModelExecutorFindTensor(slots, "logits")
    assert(IsOk(sutLogitsTensor), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: find logits slot")
    let sutReplayLogits = Value(sutLogitsTensor)

    # --- SUT official entry point (same function DistributedGenerateGreedyDenseTransformerTokens
    # calls) -- must agree with both the manual replay above and the
    # independent oracle, bit for bit ---
    let executed = mexec.ModelExecutorExecuteDenseTransformerTokens(graph, fixture.bindings, fixture.store, promptTokenIds)
    assert(IsOk(executed), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut forward execution")
    let sutOutput = Value(executed)
    echo(strutil.Join(["sut logits: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString(sutOutput.logits.data)], ""))
    assert(sutOutput.logits.shape.len == 2 && sutOutput.logits.shape[0] == 2 && sutOutput.logits.shape[1] == vocabSize,
           " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut logits shape")
    assert(sutOutput.logits.scale == HfDgRefScale,
           " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut logits scale")
    for i in 0..<sutOutput.logits.data.len:
        assert(sutOutput.logits.data[i] == sutReplayLogits.data[i],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut tokens-entry-point vs sut op-replay logits")
        assert(sutOutput.logits.data[i] == oracleLogits.vals[i],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut logits vs independent oracle logits")

    # --- greedy generate loop: SUT (DistributedGenerateGreedyDenseTransformerTokens)
    # vs independent oracle (HfDgRefGenerateGreedy), same no-kv-cache /
    # full-recompute-per-step / argmax-with-earliest-tie-wins contract ---
    let maxNewTokens: int32 = 2
    let oracleGenerated = HfDgRefGenerateGreedy(oraclePromptIds, maxNewTokens, -1, oracleWeights, attentionHeads, keyValueHeads, headDim, HfDgRefRopeTheta())
    echo(strutil.Join(["oracle generate: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString(oracleGenerated)], ""))
    let sutGenerated = engine.DistributedGenerateGreedyDenseTransformerTokens(
        graph, fixture.bindings, fixture.store, promptTokenIds, maxNewTokens, -1)
    assert(IsOk(sutGenerated), " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut generate ok")
    let sutGeneratedTokens = Value(sutGenerated)
    echo(strutil.Join(["sut generate: ", HfDgRefIntArrayToString(sutGeneratedTokens.data)], ""))
    assert(sutGeneratedTokens.shape.len == 1 && sutGeneratedTokens.shape[0] == oracleGenerated.len,
           " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut/oracle generate token count")
    for i in 0..<oracleGenerated.len:
        assert(sutGeneratedTokens.data[i] == oracleGenerated[i],
               " model executor dense hf shape golden ref: sut/oracle generated token sequence")

    echo(" model_executor_dense_hf_shape_golden_ref ok")
    return 0
